{'symbol': 'PCG', 'date': '2020-06-26 03:30:00', 'title': 'PG&E PRICES OFFERINGS OF ITS COMMON STOCK AND EQUITY UNITS', 'text': 'PRICES OFFERINGS OF ITS COMMON STOCK AND EQUITY UNITS.HAS PRICED PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED UNDERWRITTEN PUBLIC OFFERING OF 423,372,629 SHARES OF ITS COMMON STOCK AT A PRICE PER SHARE TO PUBLIC OF $9.50.PRICED PREVIOUSLY ANNOUNCED CONCURRENT UNDERWRITTEN PUBLIC OFFERING OF 14,545,455 OF ITS EQUITY UNITS AT A PRICE OF $100 PER UNIT.TOTAL NET PROCEEDS TO CORPORATION, BEFORE ESTIMATED OFFERING EXPENSES, OF ABOUT $3.968 BILLION AND ABOUT $1.186 BILLION, RESPECTIVELY.OFFERINGS ARE PART OF PG&E\'S PLAN TO FUND ITS EMERGENCE FROM CHAPTER 11, SUBJECT TO MARKET CONDITIONS.PG&E HAS APPLIED TO LIST EQUITY UNITS ON NEW YORK STOCK EXCHANGE UNDER SYMBOL "PCGU".EXPECTS AMOUNT PAYABLE PER EQUITY UNIT PER FULL QUARTER IN RESPECT OF THE RELEVANT ZERO-COUPON U.S. TREASURY STRIPS WILL BE EQUAL TO $1.3750.'}